  "question": {
    "text": "A circular coil is placed near a current carrying conductor, both lying on the plane of the paper. The current is flowing through the conductor in such a way that the induced current in the loop is clockwise as shown in the figure. The current in the wire is,\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/rs1OIqN6mLeEe1nW-twqsJXSDUlQ55UR4ePCD19S514.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2kw4g",
      "text": "time dependent and downward.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xwuQZ",
      "text": "steady and upward.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YQn0U",
      "text": "An alternating current.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "g8usP",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint : If current is increasing in upward direction, so magnetic field is increasing in out of plane in order to oppose it induced current will be in clockwise direction\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/V7_WflNIFdTzwNmODCrVksKg4JXebG9Wlp4XI-sFO4M.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nSimilarly if current is decreasing in downward direction, so magnetic field is decreasing into the plane in order to support it induced current will be in clockwise direction.",
    "image": null
  },
